<title>ITALY: L'Espresso '96 cons net profit rises.</title>
<headline>L'Espresso '96 cons net profit rises.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1997-03-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ending December 31, 1996.</p>
<p>(In billion lire unless stated)</p>
<p>    Cons net profit		   29.4	vs     12.5</p>
<p>    Gross operating margin	 140.2	vs     98.4</p>
<p>    Cons turnover		   1,254.5     vs  1,119.2</p>
<p>    Parent net profit		  18.6     vs	0.7</p>
<p>    Dividend			     150 lire vs    none</p>
<p>    Parent turnover		   158.6     (up 16.7 pct)</p>
<p>    Gross operating margin	   13.7     vs	6.3</p>
<p>    Net equity			   536.4    vs   n/a</p>
<p>Note - Espresso group said its net fiancial position at the end of 1996 was positive at 58.5 billion compared with a negative position of 10.2 billion a year previously.</p>
<p>Espresso group which is controlled by financier Carlo De Benedetti's industrial holding CIR also gave parent and consolidated results for its subsidiary, publisher Editoriale La Repubblica SPa.</p>
<p>La Repubblica net consolidated profit was 20.2 billion against 2.4 billion previously, with turnover 673 billion, up 17.9 percent and a gross operating margin of 85.1 billion versus 57.6 billion previously.</p>
<p>The parent company made a net profit of 25.2 billion compared with a 1995 loss of 2.3 billion, on a turnover of 614.7 billion versus 529.5 billion previously.</p>
<p>--Milan bureau +392 66129507</p>
</text>
